# Breaking changes to the API's spec that a reviewer accepted (CR-007 R19.2), read by
# scripts/api_breaking.sh as oasdiff's --err-ignore: one line per change, "METHOD PATH
# description", exactly as oasdiff prints it. Lines starting with # match nothing.
#
# Add a line only for a change that doesn't change the wire, and say why above it. A line
# matters only while the base spec still has the old shape: once its pull request merges,
# remove it with the next change to this file.
#
# S1 (2026-11-15): the 422s described FastAPI's HTTPValidationError (`detail` an array),
# a shape this API never sent: it sends problem details, `detail` a string. A client
# generated from the old spec was already wrong; the spec now says what the API does.
